  "summary": "The study fabricated three distinct micro-supercapacitor electrode systems: an asymmetric Ti3C2Tx/rGO interdigitated MSC, an asymmetric Ti3C2Tx/rGO sandwich MSC, and an all-Ti3C2Tx symmetric interdigitated control. Ti3C2Tx was synthesized by LiF/HCl minimally intensive layer delamination and both materials were spray-coated onto PET; the reported films were approximately 300 nm thick. The headline asymmetric interdigitated MSC delivered 2.4 mF cm\u22122 and 80 F cm\u22123 at 2 mV s\u22121 in 1 M PVA/H2SO4 gel electrolyte. Numerical capacitance values for the sandwich and symmetric controls were not printed in the supplied paper text, although their cycling retention and comparative Ragone behavior were shown."
